  "articleBodyHtml": "<h2>A Sudden Shock</h2>\n<p>The speaker experiences a sudden and alarming event, possibly a shock or surprise. This moment is marked by a quick reaction, as seen in the exclamation &#x27;Ah!&#x27; followed by &#x27;Eh?&#x27; and the realization that &#x27;It&#x27;s close.&#x27; These reactions suggest a moment of surprise or fear, possibly in response to an unexpected situation or object approaching rapidly.</p>\n<h2>Fear and Uncertainty</h2>\n<p>The speaker is attempting to control their fear and is seeking guidance on what to do in a dangerous situation. They express their fear by saying, &#x27;I was trying not to scream,&#x27; and they acknowledge the danger by stating, &#x27;It&#x27;s really dangerous outside.&#x27; They then ask, &#x27;Okay, what should I do?&#x27; indicating a need for help or direction in a tense moment.</p>\n<h2>A Logistical Problem</h2>\n<p>The speaker is confronted with a logistical problem – a large amount of luggage – and expresses a lack of knowledge about how to proceed. They say, &#x27;I don&#x27;t know,&#x27; and mention, &#x27;There&#x27;s still a lot of luggage,&#x27; followed by another &#x27;Eh?&#x27; which suggests confusion or hesitation in the face of this challenge.</p>\n<h2>Fear and Revelation</h2>\n<p>ひなた is scared, as indicated by the statement &#x27;I&#x27;m scared.&#x27; This shows a clear emotional response to the situation. She then begins to explain, saying, &#x27;I was only...&#x27; which suggests she is trying to convey something important, possibly an explanation or a memory.</p>\n<h2>A Revelation and Shock</h2>\n<p>ひなた confirms something by saying &#x27;Yes.&#x27; She then reveals that &#x27;It was Hannibal outside,&#x27; indicating that the danger or surprise was not from an unknown source but from a specific person. She continues, &#x27;Outside is...&#x27; and then says, &#x27;It was a festival.&#x27; This revelation changes the context of the situation, suggesting that the danger was not as it initially seemed.</p>\n<h2>A Moment of Realization</h2>\n<p>ひなた is shocked by the revelation, as seen in her exclamation, &#x27;Oh, my God.&#x27; She then reflects on the situation, saying, &#x27;It was a wonderful carnival until the end,&#x27; indicating that the event had a positive beginning but ended in a way that was unexpected or even alarming.</p>\n<h2>記事情報</h2>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fLHjpTRn6Uc</p>",
